  "body": "## What changed\n- Windows taskbar showed no CamCraft icon. winit 0.30 on Windows sets only `ICON_SMALL` (title bar) from `with_window_icon`. The taskbar button and Alt+Tab use `ICON_BIG`.\n- New `app_icon::with_icons` sets the window icon and, on Windows only, the taskbar icon (`with_taskbar_icon`, `ICON_BIG`) from `assets/logo/icons/camcraft-256.png`.\n- `shell_window.rs` now builds the window attributes through `with_icons`.\n- The exe resource (`build.rs`, `winresource`) was already in main. No `build.rs`, dependency or script change. Linux and macOS code is unchanged.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- app_icon`: both tests pass. New test `the_taskbar_icon_decodes_at_256_and_both_icons_reach_the_window_attributes` pins the 256 px decode and the window attributes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Screenshots are owed. Agents do not start the GUI, so nobody looked at the taskbar, title bar or Alt+Tab on Windows. A hand check on Windows is owed.\n- If the icon is still missing after this change, the cause is the exe resource. The resource compiler may be missing on that build machine (`build.rs` only warns).\n\nChangelog: fix(ui): the CamCraft icon shows in the Windows taskbar and Alt+Tab (#1754)\nEffort: medium\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1754\n",
